  ▐ aura  The trace patch didn't intercept (calls go through the module-level `_operators` dict), but I have enough evidence. The picture is clear:

**Root cause** — `_cstack` (the `&` operator) in `separable.py`, line 245:
```python
cright[-right.shape[0]:, -right.shape[1]:] = 1
```
When the right operand of `&` is a nested CompoundModel, `_separable` recurses and passes its precomputed matrix as `right` — but this line discards it and fills the whole block with 1s, entangling rows. It only goes unnoticed when that matrix happens to be all-ones (e.g. `Sine1D() + Linear1D(2)` → `_arith_oper` returns all-ones). System astropy 6.0.0 has exactly this line as `= right`. My battery confirmed 3 wrong cases in the checkout, all `&` with a compound on the right.

