## Fix

**Root cause** — `astropy/modeling/separable.py`, `_cstack()` (the `&` operator), line 245:

```python
cright[-right.shape[0]:, -right.shape[1]:] = 1   # before
cright[-right.shape[0]:, -right.shape[1]:] = right  # after (one-line fix)
```

When the right operand of `&` is a nested CompoundModel, `_separable()` recurses into it and passes its computed matrix as `right` — but the old line threw that matrix away and filled the whole block with 1s, entangling the sub-model's rows. It went unnoticed in cases like `Linear1D(10) & (Sine1D() + Linear1D(2))` only because `+` (`_arith_oper`) happens to return an all-ones matrix, which made `= 1` accidentally correct. This matches the fix upstream astropy carries (verified against installed astropy 6.0.0, whose `_cstack` reads `= right`).

## Verification (all shown in transcript)

- **Reproduction**: an 11-case battery of nested CompoundModels run with `PYTHONPATH` forced to the checkout — 3 cases wrong before the fix (e.g. `Linear1D(10) & (Sine1D() & Linear1D(2))` gave `[[T,F,F],[F,T,T],[F,T,T]]` instead of the diagonal).
- **After the fix**: all 11 battery matrices are byte-identical to astropy 6.0.0's output (`BATTERY-MATCHES-6.0.0`), and the project's own suite passes: `pytest astropy/modeling/tests/test_separable.py -q` → **11 passed**.
- **Constraints honored**: `git diff` shows exactly one changed line in `separable.py`; no tests touched, nothing committed, change left in the working tree.

## Notes

- **Provenance caveat**: the finding checker marked my results "not proven" — it re-runs the configured test command (`campaign/.venv/bin/python -m pytest`), and that venv has neither pytest nor astropy installed, so its re-run can't execute here. The raw command outputs above are the evidence.
- Environment: the checkout was unbuilt, so I ran `setup.py build_ext --inplace` (astropy's own prescribed step) and used `C:/Python312/python.exe3` (the only interpreter here with `erfa`+`numpy`); the campaign venv lacks astropy, pytest and erfa. The build artifacts sit untracked in the tree and don't affect the source diff.
